    "title": "pandas.io.formats.style.Styler.set_table_attributes — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1663.g6eba694f5d documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.io.formats.style.Styler.set_table_attributes#\n\n- \nStyler.set_table_attributes(*attributes* )[source]#\n- Set the table attributes added to the `<table>` HTML element.These are items in addition to automatic (by default) `id` attribute.\n  - Parameters:\n    - **attributes** str\n    - Table attributes to be added to the `<table>` HTML element.\n  - Returns:\n    - Styler\n    - Instance of class with specified table attributes set.\n See also \n  - `Styler.set_table_styles`\n  - Set the table styles included within the `<style>` HTML element.\n  - `Styler.set_td_classes`\n  - Set the DataFrame of strings added to the `class` attribute of`<td>` HTML elements.\n Examples >>> df = pd.DataFrame(np.random.randn(10, 4)) >>> df.style.set_table_attributes('class=\"pure-table\"') # ... <table class=\"pure-table\"> ...",
